  "body": "This adds four exact U8 B-stage shear rewrites and a complete finite verifier. The previously submitted head omitted `verify.py` and its source pins; this update publishes them and reproduces the original result certificate byte for byte, addressing [Doug Colkitt's review](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1115#issuecomment-6161594838).\n\nFor distinct registers, four fragments beginning at B indices 176, 194, 204 and 278 are replaced exactly:\n\n```text\nx += a*s; y += q*x; x -= a*s\n    -> y += q*x; y += (q*a)*s\n```\n\n## Result\n\n- B-stage operations: **1,918 \u2192 1,914**.\n- Scalar macros saved per orientation: **4**.\n- Forward real-component primitive bound: **193,306 \u2192 193,254**.\n- Backward real-component primitive bound: **193,354 \u2192 193,302**.\n- Exact arbitrary input columns: **728**; paid rank profile preserved.\n- Rewrite negative controls rejected: **9**.\n- No new kappa or selected-frontier change.\n\n## Complete replay and inputs\n\n`SOURCES.json` declares the immutable input closure: the already committed `research/community-frontier942-audit/t37-replay.tar.gz` (SHA-256 `48285025105210b56a32d3d4d57a21b7591760acc709d38073e4dca339eb06fe`) and the exact hashes of its canonical word, baseline emitted programs, and baseline receipts. The canonical-word digest remains `387a2266ffe006d20042221d967f67a4b18d9bb8de1cd1e01d4031b539fa74a5`.\n\nThe primary verifier uses only the standard library, reads pinned regular archive members without extraction, and imports no construction code. It checks each local identity and both complete B-stage maps with exact rational arithmetic, regenerates both baseline programs, compares the baseline receipts, and recomputes the candidate maps and primitive invoices. Its result must match the original `RESULT.json` byte for byte.\n\nThe package test exercises normal and optimized isolated Python, relocation with only the package and declared archive, and four rejection controls: missing source pins, mutated archive bytes, a wrong member pin, and changed result bytes. These checks remain active under `-O`.\n\n## Reproduce and validation\n\nPython 3.10+ and the standard library:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/u8-b-cancellation-seed32/verify.py\npython3 -I -B research/u8-b-cancellation-seed32/test_package.py\n```\n\nBoth commands pass. Normal, optimized, and relocated results match the committed certificate exactly. The updated PR applies cleanly to main at `ae95f60feec79897b153dba6459bb3f9fd4d7b8e`, where the optimized package test also passes. `git diff --check` is clean.\n\nThe retained local emitter and independent frame/wrapper auditor were rerun on the verified candidate. Both orientations preserve the paid profile, 728 columns, and 192-bit allowance; prefix bounds are 55/72 bits and all 25 inherited controls are rejected. `VALIDATION.json` records this evidence and the exact validation-source hashes. The README includes the additional reproduction commands.\n\n## Scope and attribution\n\nThis establishes finite B-stage equality and local admission. It does not rebuild global hosting, the complete supplier invoice, outer inequalities, all-size/compiler or realization interfaces, precision/tape or exact recovery, or analytic transfer. It claims no new kappa, practical multiplication speedup, or formal proof of the complete theorem.\n\nAssignment seed: 32, complex-supplier track. Original base: `abdc6a7002abdbcd9e21bfc5e1a795784deacfdf`.\n\nPrepared for @martinxxx9 with substantial OpenAI assistance. The complete verifier and input pins were reconstructed and published with OpenAI Codex assistance in response to the review. Retain Jonathan Capalbo (#942), Chafik Boukhalfa (#890/#741), Jeremy Kothe (#869/#870/#799), Hao Yan (#858), icekylinx, DreamingOfClouds, and the source notices' full contributor and AI-assistance attribution. New material is Apache-2.0; no independent human review is claimed.\n",
